UPDATE chapter_templates SET reference_content_female = E'There is probably no stronger attribute that a person can have than the ability to forgive and ask for forgiveness. In many instances it is just a very small action on your part and a huge impact on the people you love and even those you don''t. The inability to forgive is much harder on you than it will ever be on the other person. The reason is that when you don''t forgive, you give up control of your peace, joy, and, sometimes, sanity to either the other person or the action that occurred. That is too hard and way too much to give away.\n\nThe most challenging forgiveness for me is forgiving myself. I have found that it is much easier to forgive others than to forgive myself. There are things that I have done in my life that I am not proud of and the guilt from some of those actions can be debilitating if I let them. I can not. You can not either. You need to forgive yourself as well as others.\n\nThe bible is pretty clear on forgiveness. God knows that we are going to sin and He knows that we are going to need His forgiveness. He also knows how powerful forgiveness is for us both the person asking and the person giving it. Do not underestimate its power. It will set you free.\n\nIn many cases it is better to forgive and forget. It is not always possible but it is always better. In some instances though, the action that needs forgiving is large enough to learn from it. You can forgive a person and at the same time learn a powerful lesson from the circumstance. You can forgive someone and decide that the relationship is no longer good for you. Both are okay. The action of forgiving someone does not make you weak. In fact, it is one of the most powerful things you can do. Forgiveness is strength.' WHERE chapter_number = 1;